# CH07 — To Borrow Sky. Skychain Viaduct, Corren, the Chain Roc, High Aerie.

@scene D06_CREW
say pilot | Maintenance crew, Skychain anchors. We'd reset them ourselves if the captain let us up.
say worker | Captain says it's a one-person job. Captain's brother volunteered. Of course he did.
@end

@scene D06_CORREN_MEET once
say corren | Travellers. The Skychain's closed. Anchors failed in the last storm.
say corren | I'm going up alone to reset them. One leap from the high anchor to the nest, a few turns of the capstan, and the span holds.
say nera | And if you miss the leap?
say corren | Then High Aerie adds a name to the memorial and sends the next one. It's an honourable way to fall.
say nera | There's room on those anchors for a whole maintenance crew. Why is it a one-person job?
say corren | ...Because it always has been.
say dain | We're crossing anyway. Come with us. Bring the crew.
say corren | The ballast yard locks steady the wind lanes. The crew knows the locks.
say corren | Fine. We go together. I'll still take the nest myself.
say oriel | We'll see.
join C03
say narr | Corren's Aerial techniques leave the field and strike on landing. While airborne he can't be targeted.
objective corren | Cross the Skychain: lock the ballast in the yard, then cross the span to the Chain Nest.
@end

@scene D06_BALLAST1
if flag:d06_b1 done
sfx FX010
set d06_b1
say narr | The first ballast lock drops into place. Across the span, the west half of the middle lane goes still.
end
label done
say narr | The ballast lock is set.
@end

@scene D06_BALLAST2
if flag:d06_b2 done
sfx FX010
set d06_b2
say narr | The second lock seats with a groan of chain. The east half of the middle lane calms.
end
label done
say narr | The ballast lock is set.
@end

@scene D06_ROC once
music silence
say narr | The Chain Nest. A great grey bird is chained to the anchor ring, its wings holding the whole span level.
say corren | The Chain Roc. They tethered it here as a stabiliser. It's been holding the bridge up for years.
say tessa | A living anchor. Of course it is. Everything here is somebody's body holding something up.
say corren | If I cut the tether mid-leap, the span drops. If I don't, it keeps screaming.
say nera | Or the crew holds the alternate cable while you cut. Like we discussed. Like adults.
say narr | The Roc strains against its chain. A shadow sweeps across the front row.
battle B06 noflee
set b06_done
music M021
say narr | The Roc slumps against the anchor, exhausted. The crew's alternate cable is already rigged, taut and steady.
say corren | ...The span's holding.
say nera | Because six people are holding it. Cut the tether.
say narr | Corren cuts the chain. The Roc beats its wings once, twice, and lifts away into the cloud. Nobody falls.
say corren | I was supposed to - there was supposed to be a leap.
say oriel | You survived something you expected to die for. That can be disorienting.
xp 260
objective | Continue to the High Landing, north-east of the nest.
@end

@scene CH07_LANDING once
say narr | The High Landing. The crew is already bolting the new anchors into the rock, cheering in bursts.
say corren | They're going to want to put me on a wall.
say dain | Which wall?
say corren | The memorial. For nearly dying.
say nera | You didn't nearly die. You did a maintenance shift.
say corren | ...I don't know how to be thanked for that.
chapter CH07
set cable_open
say narr | High Aerie's cable ferry now runs west across the chasm toward the Pale Basin and Nacre.
objective corren | Visit High Aerie (north), then take the cable ferry west to the Pale Basin.
discover L_T05
rumor | Corren says the wind shrine above High Aerie's stair is older than the Crown.
level_floor 15
@end

@scene T05_SHRINE once
say narr | At the wind shrine the cloths stream east. Something wide and dark glides out of the cloud: a manta of storm and sky.
say "Sky Manta" | The Roc is free. It hunted me from this shrine for years, chained. I was never the anchor. You unchained the anchor.
say "Sky Manta" | I will ride your wind when you call.
vestige V04
@end

@scene T05_EDDA
if ch:CH09,!flag:accord_aerie accord
if ch:CH07 after
say edda | Captain Edda Hale. Corren's sister and supervisor. The Skychain's closed until the anchors are reset.
end
label accord
say edda | The evidence from the vault - Corren told me. The cable ferry runs on a relay under the court. If that relay goes silent, every basket stops mid-chasm.
say edda | I need transit that doesn't depend on something screaming under my feet. Can your machinist do anything?
say ivo | The cable brake by the operator's post. If I give it a counterweight governor, the baskets hold without the relay.
end
label after
say edda | You brought my brother back with a crew behind him. I don't have a ceremony for that. I should.
@end

@scene T05_OLD_PILOT
say pilot | Forty years flying rescue baskets. I'll tell you a secret: the ceremonial uniforms make safe landings harder.
say pilot | All that cloth. Looks grand falling. Snags on everything landing.
@end

@scene T05_CABLE_OP
if ch:CH07 run
say worker | Cable ferry's stopped until the Skychain anchors are sorted.
end
label run
say worker | Cable ferry's running west to the basin. Board at the chasm edge on the world road, west of the court.
@end

@scene T05_KID
say child | When I grow up I'm going to fall off something really high. For the wall.
say corren | Or you could fly rescue and come home for supper.
say child | ...Can I do both?
say corren | No.
@end

@scene T05_WIDOW
say elder | My son is on the memorial. I'd trade the wall for one more supper.
@end

@scene T05_TRAINEE
say "Trainee" | We practise the heroic leap every morning. We never practise the landing.
@end

@scene T05_HALL_INN
say elder | Returners' hall. Beds for crews coming back from the cliffs. Most nights, there's room.
inn
@end
